@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Row enter animation and reduced motion
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "User" as user
participant "Browser" as browser
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (UI components)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoComposerComponent" as composer
  participant "TodoListComponent" as list
  participant "TodoItemComponent" as item
end box
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoStore" as store
end box
user -> composer : Submit a valid title
composer -> store : addTask(title) through TodoPageComponent
store -> store : Insert { id: tmp-<uuid>, pending: true } at the top of the todos signal
store --> list : visibleTodos changes
list -> item : Create a row for the new id only, track todo.id; only pending rows animate in (L2-024)
note right of list
  Existing rows keep their DOM and do not re-animate (L2-024)
end note
item -> item : Mark the new row as entering (L2-024)
item -> browser : Request the enter animation
browser -> browser : Evaluate prefers-reduced-motion
alt No reduced-motion preference
  browser --> user : One slide-and-fade of 250 ms or less, ease-out, transform and opacity only (L2-024)
else prefers-reduced-motion is reduce
  browser --> user : Row appears with no movement, at most an opacity change of 100 ms (L2-024)
end
store -> store : On 201, drop the pending task (no exit animation) and insert the server task
store --> list : visibleTodos changes
list -> list : Track key unchanged, row DOM kept, no second enter animation (L2-024)
@enduml
